      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T21:07:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We currently use the \"sampled texture\" type for both readonly-storage and sampled-type textures, which doesn\u0027t have a way to specify \"readonly\", since a sampled texture binding doesn\u0027t allow writes (see the API declarations here: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:out/Debug/gen/third_party/dawn/include/dawn/webgpu_cpp.h;l\u003d2144;drc\u003dc410120011084508641f34a24d77d7625bd4f4bf)\n\nIn theory we would want to set read-only for the \"storageTexture\" binding type if we were using that here but WGSL 1.0 only supports write-only storage textures. There is a proposal to add support for `read_write` access but not readonly as far as I\u0027m aware: go/wgsl-rw-storage-textures.",
      "parentUuid": "5ce036c0_d44c7fe9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "758db7f264b29d8e13be9c8298f95896a20d8bf5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "beef9b2c_f7372f4e",
