      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T15:26:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does the ComputeStep and DispatchGroup bindings guarantee that a texture bound to a `kStorageTexture` resource will have the default storage texture format?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 107,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "758db7f264b29d8e13be9c8298f95896a20d8bf5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57d6eb35_80766435",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnComputePipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T21:07:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question: if the texture is internally allocated by DispatchGroup then yes, it will honor the type returned by `ComputeStep::calculateTextureParameters()`. I don\u0027t think they provide a guarantee if the texture is externally assigned via `ComputeStep::assignSharedTexture()`.\n\nI went ahead and added a debug assertion to `DispatchGroup::Builder::appendStep` just in case (binding a mismatching texture here should lead to a validation error regardless - unless we turn that off sometimes?).\n\nAs for the shader source itself it\u0027s up to the ComputeStep to declare the SkSL properly using the color format syntax proposed in go/samplers-and-storage-textures-in-sksl. That syntax isn\u0027t yet supported though and SPIR-V codegen currently assumes the texture format is compatible with a rgba8unorm texture view.",
      "parentUuid": "beef9b2c_f7372f4e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 107,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "758db7f264b29d8e13be9c8298f95896a20d8bf5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
